{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>Will Joseph hate us</b> When they returned from burying their father, Joseph passed by the pit into which they had cast him, and blessed and said: Blessed is He who performed for me a miracle in this place. They said: He still remembers what we did to him. Some say: לו ישטמנו יוסף — would that Joseph hate us in his heart and not do a deed against us; and if he wishes to do, let him repay us all the evil we repaid him — for what did we do to him? We caused that he become king, because we sold him, and the matter turned out that he became king in Egypt; so may he do to us."], :book :genesis, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 50, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Kitzur Baal HaTurim" "http://sefaria.org"] ["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:18:53.230094536Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}